46	/**
47	 * This class is a container of multiple thread pools, each for a volume,
48	 * so that we can schedule async disk operations easily.
49	 * 
50	 * Examples of async disk operations are deletion of block files.
51	 * We don't want to create a new thread for each of the deletion request, and
52	 * we don't want to do all deletions in the heartbeat thread since deletion
53	 * can be slow, and we don't want to use a single thread pool because that
54	 * is inefficient when we have more than 1 volume.  AsyncDiskService is the
55	 * solution for these.
56	 * Another example of async disk operation is requesting sync_file_range().
57	 * 
58	 * This class and {@link org.apache.hadoop.util.AsyncDiskService} are similar.
59	 * They should be combined.
